   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to hospital domestic\nviolence policies and procedures; and to amend a chapter of the laws of 2019\namending the public health law relating to hospital domestic violence policies\nand procedures as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 3962-A and A.\n2850-A, in relation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7192",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7192-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2805-z, Pub Health L; amd §2, Chap of 2019 (as proposed in S.3962-A & A.2850-A)",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7192\n\nSPONSOR: SALAZAR\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to hospital domestic\nviolence policies and procedures; and to amend a chapter of the laws of\n2019 amending the public health law relating to hospital domestic\nviolence policies and procedures as proposed in legislative bills\nnumbers S. 3962-A and A. 2850-A, in relation to the effectiveness there-\nof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of\nL.2019,c.733.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation clarifies that only nursing, medical, social work and\nother clinical personnel, and security personnel working in hospital\nservice units must receive training on the hospital's domestic violence\npolicy. The bill also requires the Commissioner of Health to\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPursuant to approval memo 79 of 2019, the Executive expressed concerns\nthat changes would be needed to clarify the hospital's role related to\nthese domestic violence policies and procedures. The bill also clarifies\nthat a designated staff member of the hospital must contact a domestic\nviolence or victim assistance organization that is identified by the\nCommissioner of Health in the hospital's geographic area.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 733 of the Laws of 2019.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
